<p>Follow these steps to save printing preferences settings registered 
 to a one click preset as a file.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>The following features settings are not stored 
 for one click presets.</p></li>
</ul>
<p class="Normal-ol"><span class="Term-Soft">User ID</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">File 
 Name</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Password</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">User 
 Name</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Classification Code</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">User 
 Code</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Login User Name</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Login 
 Password</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Folder Password</span>, watermark 
 items except <span class="Term-Soft">Print Watermark</span> (On/Off) and 
 selected watermark name, overlay items except <span class="Term-Soft">Add 
 Overlay</span> (On/Off) and selected overlay name, bitmap items except 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Add Bitmap</span> (On/Off) and selected bitmap name, 
 color profile items except selected color profile name.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Manage...</span> on 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used Settings</span> tab. The <span class="Term-Soft">Manage One Click Preset List</span> dialog box appears.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the one click preset name which you want 
 to save as a file, and then click <span class="Term-Soft">Export...</span>.<br/>
 The <span class="Term-OS">Save As</span> dialog box appears.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-OS">File name:</span> box, 
 enter the file name to save the settings.<br/>
 The file name extension is ".json".</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-OS">Save</span>.<br/>
 The dialog box closes and the setting is saved.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Manage One Click Preset List</span> dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
